ch each of  these things collectively together would  weigh so let's have a quick think about  what a pyramid of biomass would look  like for this particular food chain now  the bottom part of a food chain the  bottom part of a soil the bottom part of  a pyramid of biomass is always the  producer so we start with a producer and  then we work our way up different  trophic levels okay now let's say these  plants here so these are our plants  let's say they weighed a thousand  kilograms so all of these plants  eaten by the roads with a thousand  kilograms how much mass where our  rabbits have would it be the same would  it be more or wood even less now the  answer is less now this is because this  is because energy is lost from this  stage to this stage so as a result we  can't have exactly the same mass of  rabbits being able to survive off these  plants similarly when we transfer the  energy from the rabbit to the Fox and a  higher trophic level on a higher trophic  level we've again got a lower mass again  because energy is lost at this stage so  if energy wasn't lost these we wouldn't  necessarily have to have less mass each  time but because energy is lost the  higher up we go so the higher trophic  levels will have a smaller mass so that  is basically how energy and biomass  works I think
 

